  "rm": false,
  "notes": "New group [2,2,2,16]. The curve is the Howe–Leprévost–Poonen (2,2)-gluing (HLP 2000, Prop. 4) of E1 = E_{2,4}(t) with torsion [2,4] (conductor 2781739260113226584010) and E2 = E_{2,8}(u) with torsion [2,8] (conductor 477491580510), in the Tate normal forms of HLP Table 3, at u = -20/31, t = -4333968559/38784504316. The gluing is the identity on the labelled 2-torsion points, and the Kummer images of the rational torsion of E1 and E2 agree completely (gain 4), which gives #J(Q)_tors = 2 * 4 * 4 * 4 = 128. The point was found by a fibre-wise 2-descent: over fixed u the gain locus is a 2-covering of y^2 = x^3 - d^2 x, here with d = 554577910 and a point of canonical height 22.83. The two elliptic quotients of the curve are Q-isomorphic to E1 and E2, and j(E1) != j(E2). Output of pipeline/magma/prepare_submission.m (Magma V2.29-4): J(Q)_tors = [2,2,2,16]; gcd of #J(F_p) over 25 good primes = 128 (sharp); J(F_11) = [2,2,2,16]; conductor N(E1) N(E2) = 1328257075878182563154683193645100 (J is isogenous over Q to E1 x E2). Further points on the same fibre give more curves with the same torsion subgroup (checked for one more, from 3P).",
